  "limits": [
    "The sequence is the read's own published readings, not a subscription log: each record carries the last emission the read held when that record was dispatched, so an emission that arrived and was replaced between two records would not appear here. The drive's second subscription (capture.observer) watches the same stream from outside the read and is recorded beside the sequence, never in place of it: it emitted false at 100.6 ms and true at 129.8 ms, the same two values the two records published.",
    "The drive is a page load of the lazy route, not a click: the router's own initial navigation to /lazy holds a pending task (its loadChildren import) while the read attaches at document_idle, and releases it at NavigationEnd. The route, the arrival list and the task's release are the page's own evidence; isStable carries no task id, so no cause is recorded.",
    "A client-side navigation after a settle cannot produce this reading: capture.controls.stableAtAttach measured it. That page was stable at attach, and the section's settle stayed at the attach reading across a router navigation whose false and true the same stream emitted later. The settle field records the first true at or after attach and never moves again, which is why the drive had to attach while the page was still unstable.",
    "One page, one browser, one fixture at this head. The three reproductions are the same drive repeated, not three pages, and each produced its own transition.",
